lib/IO/K8s/Role/Resource.pm:136-139 -- the is_array_of_str /
is_hash_of_str (and raw array/hash attribute) branches pass the
attribute reference through uncopied. Post-processing the struct from
TO_JSON/object_to_struct silently mutates the object, and the mutation
shows up in every later serialization.

Repro (measured): $cm->TO_JSON->{data}{key} = "MUTATED" changes
$cm->data->{key}; push @{$container->TO_JSON->{command}}, "EXTRA"
changes $container->command. The object branches (is_array_of_objects
etc.) are clean via map; only the scalar containers alias.

Fix sketch: shallow-copy in the ARRAY/HASH pass-through branches
([@$value] / {%$value}). Note deep structures under raw hash attributes
would still alias one level down -- decide and document the depth.

Cross-reference: the symmetric input side exists in
IO::K8s::_inflate_struct -- inflated objects share references with the
input struct (measured: mutating the source struct changes the object).
Same decision should cover both directions or explicitly scope to output.

Found in the 2026-08-18 core-module review (repro verified).
Lane: io-k8s-worker, then io-k8s-test-writer.
